**Site Report – Station T-08, Survey Area T**

The VES interpretation at T-08 yields a 5-layer resistivity model. Resistivity decreases slightly from Layer 1 (225.6 Ω·m) to Layer 2 (217.6 Ω·m), then rises sharply through Layers 3 and 4 (626.8 and 694.3 Ω·m), before dropping again at Layer 5 (580.5 Ω·m). This sequence—decrease, then increase, then increase, then decrease—corresponds to curve segments H (1-2-3), A (2-3-4), and K (3-4-5), giving an overall HAK-type curve. This matches the classification on file. The subsurface likely reflects a moderately resistive near-surface unit overlying a more resistive, possibly compact or cemented zone, with a lower-resistivity unit at depth, consistent with a layered aquifer system. No discrepancies were found between the computed curve type and the filed classification.

